ency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.11513515053901058,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":86.1,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.013815636942771678,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":26.5,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.12481755261547153,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.36492002,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.75,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":75.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ridgepost Capital, Inc. operates as a multi-asset class private market solutions provider in the alternative asset management industry in the United States, North America, Europe, and internationally. The company's portfolio of private solutions includes private equity, venture capital, impact investing, and private credit, as well as primary fund of funds, secondary investment, and direct and co-investment services. It markets its private equity solutions under the RCP Advisors, Bonaccord Capital, Ridgepost Advisors, and Qualitas brands; venture capital solutions under the TrueBridge brand; impact investing solutions under the Enhanced brand; and private credit solutions under the Five Points, Hark Capital, and WTI brands. The company was formerly known as P10, Inc. and changed its name to Ridgepost Capital, Inc. in February 2026. Ridgepost Capital, Inc. was founded in 1992 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Luke A. Sarsfield III | Chairman of the Board, President & CEO | Age 51 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 326 people. Revenue per employee of $912K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 19%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $56K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $114K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Ridgepost Capital, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.2B market cap on $297M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $18M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 36% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 188% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.878245016673689},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 60% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (75% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ridgepost Capital (NYSE:RPC) Stock: Insider Andrew Rowan Nelson Sells 10,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/ridgepost-capital-nyserpc-stock-insider-andrew-rowan-nelson-sells-10000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479942.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"RPC (NYSE:RES) Hits New 1-Year Low \u2013 Here\u2019s What Hap